nodecode-channel-max is a rewrite of Realmagnum's Realmagnum/hermes-max-integration:

  https://github.com/Realmagnum/hermes-max-integration
  commit 50c7a9a7c16b6207a079b7b883718dd863e9e951
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Realmagnum / Hermes Agent community (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the MAX bot API calls the adapter makes — the long-poll read of
/updates with its marker, the message plans (POST /messages, PUT and DELETE by
message id, the typing action), the JSON shapes a message update and a sent
message are read as, the /me check a probe makes, and the pieces of a
message that name who said it and where — in Common Lisp over Nodecode's
channel kit, which supplies the session, admission and delivery machinery the
original plugin had of its own.

Left out, and why: the response by webhook (a public endpoint the operator
must expose; long polling gives the same messages without one), file, voice and
picture sending with MAX's two-step upload, voice-message transcription, the
table-to-image renderer with its optional Playwright and Chromium download,
inline keyboards and callback buttons, the bundled Russian Trusted Root CA
(Nodecode's TLS trust is the system's), and the desktop sidebar. Each is a
feature of the original's runtime rather than of the conversation, and the
first two are where a rewrite would start if operators ask for them.
